# An explicit alias set leaves the replaced copy unarmed, so stale routers
# keep writing into it.
MODULE: SupersededCopyTakesNoWriteExplicitAliasUnarmed
TARGET: SupersededCopyTakesNoWrite
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: an explicit alias set never arms the copy it replaces
PERTURBS: ExplicitPublish

--- FIND
    /\ armed' = armed \cup {<<alias, s, Other>> : s \in shards[alias]}
--- REPLACE
    /\ armed' = armed
--- END
